[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3740895374","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3740895374","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":3740895374,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7e-YiO","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-12T23:01:04Z","updated_at":"2026-01-12T23:35:38Z","body":"~Didn't test this, but from what I can see in the video attached the zoom slider should be adjusted with the scroll bar (and vice versa).~\r\n\r\nEDIT: nvm it does. I'm just blind lol sorry.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3740895374/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3740901861","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3740901861","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":3740901861,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7e-aHl","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-12T23:03:48Z","updated_at":"2026-01-12T23:03:48Z","body":"It's relatively subtle but the zoom slider does move as the scroll bar handles are dragged. I don't recall testing moving the zoom slider and watching the scroll bar handles, so I'll have to do that later","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3740901861/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3800890109","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3800890109","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":3800890109,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ijPr9","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T17:54:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T17:54:22Z","body":"Should I increase the height/thickness of this scroll bar? I've found the clickable area for the edges can be difficult to find (you can even see me miss it in the video, at one point). This would introduce a bit of inconsistency, as one scroll bar in the editor would the thicker than all the rest, but on the other hand I suppose this scroll bar is *already* different due to the grabbable edges...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3800890109/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3801372622","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3801372622","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":3801372622,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ilFfO","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T19:35:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T19:35:33Z","body":"> This would introduce a bit of inconsistency, as one scroll bar in the editor would the thicker than all the rest, but on the other hand I suppose this scroll bar is _already_ different due to the grabbable edges...\r\n\r\nI think it having handles at each end is enough to make it its own thing with its own thickness. I do think the white handles look wierd being a horizontal capsule.\r\n\r\nMaybe even some other look enhancements can validate the choice even more? (I don't have ux experience I'm just giving my opinion)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3801372622/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3877255945","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3877255945","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":3877255945,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nGjsJ","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T12:19:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:19:49Z","body":"The scroll bar is somewhat buggy after you drag it\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c227f7f8-6718-44d0-a14f-f025f6bb06da\r\n\r\nNotice how it jumps when I click it.\r\n\r\nAlso the initial zoom is wrong (when you just add AnimationPlayer and add first animation).\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f5727e5d-3c25-42c5-a75c-00e8898037e3\r\n\r\nSee what happens to the timeline.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3877255945/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3894719527","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3894719527","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":3894719527,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oJLQn","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T03:57:14Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T03:57:14Z","body":"Thanks for testing! The first bug, where the left side of the scroll bar wouldn't drag correctly if the right side was at the max value, should now be fixed.\r\n\r\nThe second bug, where the initial zoom level for a new animation doesn't match what the scroll bar enforces, is continuing to give me grief. I'm having trouble finding the code in Godot that sets the initial zoom level; the code in `AnimationTimelineEdit::set_animation()` and `AnimationTimelineEdit::_notification()` seems to be working as expected, but for some reason at first, Godot is still displaying the timeline that goes out to 10-ish seconds?\r\n\r\nI'll be able to take another look at this in the coming days, but if anyone happens to have better knowledge of how these parts of Godot are built, guidance/insight would be very appreciated! 😅","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3894719527/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3939288760","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3939288760","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":3939288760,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qzMa4","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T19:25:08Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T19:25:08Z","body":"Animation Team Discussion:\r\n\r\n1. Several bugs found by testing\r\n2. @Meorge has asked for help in the animation channel in rocketchat.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3939288760/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3939295725","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3939295725","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":3939295725,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qzOHt","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T19:30:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T19:30:54Z","body":"In my opinion, the drag handles are inaccessible because they are too small. I think that the click target of the handles / scrollbar should be as wide as the slider widget even if the widget is displayed smaller.\r\n\r\nPersonally I think Godot scrollbars are in general extremely difficult to click. This adds small handles onto an already small scrollbar.\r\n\r\nAlso, I'm curious what happens if the animation is really long (e.g. 1 hour long) and the scrollbar is too narrow. Does this prevent the tiny scrollbar from being clicked when it's overlapping with the two endpoints? (Again this might be a godot editor issue: I think godot should have a minimum size for a scrollbar but it doesn't)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3939295725/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3939576313","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3939576313","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":3939576313,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q0Sn5","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T22:01:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T22:01:46Z","body":"> Several bugs found by testing\r\n\r\nIs this referring to [the two bugs identified by KoBeWi a few weeks ago](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3877255945), or are there others as well? The first of the bugs KoBeWi found should now be fixed; the second one is still indeed an issue that needs to be resolved. If there are other bugs as well, then I can certainly look into those in the coming days.\r\n\r\n> In my opinion, the drag handles are inaccessible because they are too small. I think that the click target of the handles / scrollbar should be as wide as the slider widget even if the widget is displayed smaller.\r\n\r\nI agree; as I said [earlier](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3800890109), I was even having trouble grabbing the handles sometimes when recording my demo videos. Increasing the thickness would make them a lot easier to use. I briefly looked into how to accomplish that a few weeks ago, but didn't find any _super_ quick solution. Given that a few people have agreed now, I may give it a second, more in-depth attempt.\r\n\r\n> Also, I'm curious what happens if the animation is really long (e.g. 1 hour long) and the scrollbar is too narrow. Does this prevent the tiny scrollbar from being clicked when it's overlapping with the two endpoints? (Again this might be a godot editor issue: I think godot should have a minimum size for a scrollbar but it doesn't)\r\n\r\nThat's a good question, I haven't tested that. It's not implemented yet to my knowledge, but I could see us disabling the endpoints once the scrollbar itself is small enough, so that all mouse events just go to the regular scrollbar. Overall though, I'd probably want to try replicating this scenario in other software with this kind of scrollbar, such as Blender, and seeing how it is handled there.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3939576313/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3949084331","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3949084331","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":3949084331,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rYj6r","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T05:08:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T05:08:20Z","body":"I was able to spend some more time on this today, and I have both good news and bad news.\r\n\r\nThe good news is, I've made the scroll bar thicker so it's easier to click and drag the edges. I'll probably need to tweak the colors a bit, but overall I'm a lot happier with this!\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6430eb7e-c3d6-4912-b2db-26575c8a45fe\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe bad news is, a good solution to the initial-zoom problem continues to elude me. I _think_ what's happening here is the editor initially draws at a sort of \"default\" scale using the zoom slider's value. The existing slider's zoom bounds are different from the new scrollbar's zoom bounds. So when we go to use the scrollbar's zoom function, it clamps everything to within what the scrollbar's zoom function allows, causing that sudden jump in zoom level.\r\n\r\nAt least a good starting point would be to have the scrollbar apply its zoom to the editor as soon as a new animation is opened, so that the user doesn't see a jump. The user still unfortunately _will_ see a jump if they use the old zoom slider to zoom out farther than the scrollbar can, and then tries to use the scrollbar's edges to refine their selection.\r\n\r\nIn the long run, I think it'd probably make sense to retire the old zoom slider, and have the edges in the scrollbar be the sole visual method of editing zoom. This way there's no redundancy or potential for discontinuity between UI controls that are aiming to do the same thing. I'd like to take a look at some other software that uses this resizable scrollbar UI and see how they behave in these kinds of circumstances, as well as if they offer a dedicated zoom UI as well.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3949084331/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4189114541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-4189114541","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":4189114541,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75sNCt","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-05T16:04:55Z","updated_at":"2026-04-05T16:04:55Z","body":"Thank you very much for the review!\r\n\r\nFor the moment I think I'm more likely to go with option 1 and keep this internal for now. My time at the moment is a bit limited, and exposing this as an official GUI class (including testing, docs, and everything else that comes with it) would push this PR back substantially, I expect.\r\n\r\nThere does remain [the issue of a newly-created animation's zoom level conflicting with the scroll-bar's zoom as KoBeWi noticed](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3877255945). I explained my understanding of this bug and how I think it would be fixed [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-3949084331).\r\n\r\nIs the presence of this behavior something that the animation team would be okay with for the time being? Later on, someone could do another PR that retires the existing zoom slider and makes the zoom level entirely controlled by the resizable scroll bar so that there's no \"jump\" when the user switches between the zoom slider and the scroll bar.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4189114541/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4203185424","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-4203185424","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":4203185424,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76h4UQ","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T01:19:14Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T01:19:14Z","body":"The HResizableScrollBar code has been moved into `editor/gui`, and the theme setup has been moved to `editor/themes`. It looks good on the Modern theme, but the Classic theme has the side grabbers very wide:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"857\" height=\"550\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-04-07 at 18 17 15@2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ff3f429e-cf29-40ee-9002-d9250d8aec09\" />\r\n\r\nWill look more into that tonight.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4203185424/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4204074736","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-4204074736","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":4204074736,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76lRbw","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T05:37:43Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T05:37:43Z","body":"Classic theme looks maybe-better now, although it's now experiencing kind of the opposite problem 😅\r\n\r\n<img width=\"872\" height=\"543\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-04-07 at 22 35 50@2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e0f64bd5-c3ca-439d-a91b-ba0600f0e8d0\" />\r\n\r\nI also fixed an issue where the main grabber was being drawn a second time by the subclass, but in the process it's lost the highlight when the grabber is hovered.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4204074736/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4204799243","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-4204799243","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":4204799243,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76oCUL","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T08:16:07Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T08:18:21Z","body":"Works good. In this video the project has been just opened. The only problem I see is that the scollbar jumps to the right at 0:18 after it was compressed and I zoomed in by using the zoom slider. Don't know if it's a problem from this PR or a different problem with the animation panel.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/006ab8f1-e8e9-495f-9c0f-8740438a0dca\r\n\r\nMy current concern is that on a fullhd screen the bottom toolbar is very cluttered but that's out of the scope of this PR.\r\n(Also, I didn't know the zoom slider has the same problem of having an insane range as the sliders in the node inspector.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4204799243/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4207651996","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-4207651996","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":4207651996,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76y6yc","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T16:01:31Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T16:01:31Z","body":"Thanks for taking a look!\r\n\r\nI think the problem you encountered at 0:18 in your video is similar to the initial-zoom problem, and both are caused by a difference in how the existing editor handles zoom amounts and bounds versus the new resizable scroll bar. In the long run I think the best approach to this would be to remove the existing zoom slider and have the zoom level be handled more directly by the scroll bar. Unfortunately I'd also expect this to be a relatively massive task, and at the moment don't have much time to dive into that 😅","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4207651996/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5337509553","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-5337509553","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":5337509553,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPiPusQ","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-19T04:24:16Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T04:24:16Z","body":"Thanks for the approval!\r\n\r\nI'm aware of the issue you brought up, and unfortunately at the moment I don't know of a good but (relatively) quick way to fix it. There's an approach to storing position and zoom information that I've used for making zoomable timelines like this in other projects of mine which I think could work well here. However, replacing the current animation timeline's system with it would probably take quite a while. I may write up a proposal describing the approach and submit it sometime so we could discuss it and potentially attempt an implementation.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5337509553/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5398216825","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-5398216825","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":5398216825,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQcJAeQ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T16:29:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T16:29:11Z","body":"Original authors have been inactive enough that the original PR is now closed and properly marked as superseded","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5398216825/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5852943560","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-5852943560","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":5852943560,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXNzUyA","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-27T05:21:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-27T05:21:34Z","body":"Thanks for the review! I'm now working on refactoring its `gui_input` method so that it only contains the logic for the `ResizableScrollBar`-specific input, and passes everything else up to the `ScrollBar` parent class. There are still a few issues with it I'll have to look more into tomorrow if/when I have time (namely, the endpoints jump when dragged for some reason), but it seems to be progressing quickly! I think I also recall this bug popping up a long time ago while maintaining this PR, so I'll have to read through the history and see if I can find our discussion on it, if it did indeed exist.\r\n\r\nSince it's currently in a broken/WIP state, I'll convert it to a draft for now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5852943560/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5863596822","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#issuecomment-5863596822","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114289","id":5863596822,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXX9jFg","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-28T04:43:57Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T04:43:57Z","body":"I've now refactored the `ResizableScrollBar` class to cut out the generic `ScrollBar` duplicate logic. It's over a hundred lines shorter now, if I counted correctly!\r\n\r\nI'm hoping to more closely review the code the original authors wrote for the `AnimationTimelineEdit` in the coming days and see if there are naming or logic improvements I can make, but there aren't any definite refactors I'm planning on making there, so I'll open it back up for review.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5863596822/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]